00:00:43.735 --> 00:00:46.110
I want to honor this day by
having a discussion with some

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:48.570
of the most interesting and
trailblazing leaders in tech

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:49.392
today.

00:00:49.392 --> 00:00:50.850
There's been a lot
of research on--

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.975
I've been in the diversity
space about seven years.

00:00:52.975 --> 00:00:55.890
And over that time, I've
seen a lot of research

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.790
around the importance of
diverse and inclusive teams.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:02.040
It affects the
degree of innovation

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.800
that you have, and even
affects our bottom line.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.620
But while meaningful
change is possible ,

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:08.970
there are a lot of challenges.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:11.860
There are a lot of
barriers that we face.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.620
So we have assembled
an incredible panel

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:15.450
of five change-makers
here today,

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:18.290
to share their stories and
advice on some of the ways

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:20.900
that the tech industry
has been driving success

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:23.700
through more heterogeneous work
and inclusive environments.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.130
And I will let them
introduce themselves.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:27.360
We'll start with Bridget.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.802
BRIDGET FREY: I'm Bridget Frey,
and I'm the CTO at Redfin.

00:01:31.802 --> 00:01:33.635
JEANETTE CALANDRA: Good
afternoon, everyone.

00:01:33.635 --> 00:01:36.740
